text:
Alyssa: quick heads-up — found an interop edge between streaming NDJSON responses and our JSON-schema validator in the SDK. Clients using `Content-Type: application/x-ndjson` get parse errors when optional numeric fields are omitted vs set to null. Can we do a quick smoke-check before the canary?

Marco: repro steps? small logs plz.

Alyssa: minimal repro: server returns ndjson stream of objects, schema expects `score` as number but we allowed `null` historically. the SDK parser treats missing and null differently when content-type is ndjson. snippet:```json
# server-side schema (simplified)
{
  "type":"object",
  "properties":{
    "items":{
      "type":"array",
      "items":{
        "type":"object",
        "properties":{
          "id":{"type":"string"},
          "score":{"type":["number","null"]}
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "required":["items"]
}
```
But ndjson stream has lines like: `{"id":"x","score":null}` and also `{"id":"y"}`. SDK validator errors on the second form when content-type is ndjson but passes for `application/json`.

Priya: hmm. probably the streaming parser bails early and assumes keys present if null union exists. Two paths: (1) relax schema to allow missing (ugh), (2) make parser treat absent == null for union types during ndjson parse. I prefer (2) + add a lenient flag.

Alyssa: agreed. plan I'm proposing: server and SDK should normalize ndjson parsing to unify with non-streaming semantics. minimal change in SDK: when schema says `"type":["number","null"]`, if key missing treat as `null` for validation only. Add unit + regression for streaming vs json endpoints.

David: will that break existing consumers who rely on missing vs null distinction? Any customers doing that?

Alyssa: I scanned logs for last 30d — only internal clients in experiments. No external apps appear to rely on missing vs null for these fields (we checked a sample). We can gate behind `lenient_streaming_parse=true` defaulting to true for now and document.

Marco: can you throw up a PR? I can review quick. Also ping infra if it touches parser libs.

Alyssa: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/server/pull/4567 — includes SDK change, unit tests, and a short migration note. DeployBot: Deploy pipeline kicked off for staging.

deploy-bot: CI passed for PR #4567, deploy to staging started — build 2026.03.15-11.

Priya: I will run the regression harness against canary after staging. Will also add a small eval to catch nullable-vs-missing regressions for embeddings and chat.

Marco: LGTM from me pending tests. leaving a couple inline comments.

David: thumbs up — if Priya signs off, approve and we can canary to 5% for 2h.

Alyssa: thanks team — tagging @marco @priya for reviews. will coordinate canary window 14:00-16:00 PT tomorrow.

Marco: got it.

Priya: adding test run to calendar invite.

Alyssa: will update release notes with `lenient_streaming_parse` bit and add a doc section for SDK behavior. Done.
